Perfect! I've completed a comprehensive analysis of the TinyMCE contrast checker implementation. Here's what I found:

## 1. Location of the Contrast Checker Code

**Main implementation directory:** [plugins/tinymce/a11y/](plugins/tinymce/a11y/)

**Key files:**
- [plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts) — Main plugin implementation
- [plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/strings.ts](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/strings.ts) — Localized strings
- [plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/i18n.json](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/i18n.json) — i18n definitions
- [plugins/tinymce/a11y/tests/index.test.ts](plugins/tinymce/a11y/tests/index.test.ts) — Test suite

---

## 2. Element Selection & Text Content Detection

**How the contrast checker selects elements to test** ([index.ts, lines 220-244](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts#L220-L244)):

```typescript
appliesTo: (element) => {
  if (!(element instanceof HTMLElement)) return false;
  if (element.closest("img, svg, canvas, video, object, embed")) return false;
  const text = element.textContent?.trim() ?? "";
  if (text.length === 0) return false;  // ← Excludes empty/whitespace-only elements
  const style = window.getComputedStyle(element);
  const color = element.style.color || style.color;
  const bg = element.style.backgroundColor || style.backgroundColor;
  return color !== "" && bg !== "" && color !== "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" && bg !== "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)";
},
```

**Key points on element handling:**
- Excludes media elements: `img, svg, canvas, video, object, embed`
- **Checks `textContent?.trim().length`** — This means:
  - ✅ Elements with actual text pass (including those with inline `style="color: ..."`
  - ❌ **Icon-font spans (like `<span class="instui-icon">` with empty text content but CSS-rendered glyphs) are EXCLUDED** — because the text content check fails, the element won't even enter the test phase
  - ❌ Spans with only zero-width spaces are excluded
- **Does NOT check for `contenteditable="false"` attribute** — this won't exclude elements from the scan
- Requires both computed foreground and background colors to be present and not fully transparent

---

## 3. Contrast Checking Logic

**Color parsing & luminance calculation** ([index.ts, lines 109-159](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts#L109-L159)):

```typescript
function parseCssColor(rawColor: string | null): [number, number, number] | null {
  // Supports: hex (#fff, #ffffff), rgb(), rgba()
  // Returns null for unsupported color formats
}

function relativeLuminance(color: [number, number, number]): number {
  // WCAG AA luminance formula with gamma adjustment
  const [r, g, b] = color.map((channel) => {
    const adjusted = channel / 255;
    return adjusted <= 0.03928 ? adjusted / 12.92 : ((adjusted + 0.055) / 1.055) ** 2.4;
  });
  return 0.2126 * r + 0.7152 * g + 0.0722 * b;
}

function contrastRatio(colorA: string | null, colorB: string | null): number {
  const a = parseCssColor(colorA);
  const b = parseCssColor(colorB);
  if (!a || !b) return Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;  // ← Unparseable colors pass the check
  const luminanceA = relativeLuminance(a);
  const luminanceB = relativeLuminance(b);
  const lighter = Math.max(luminanceA, luminanceB);
  const darker = Math.min(luminanceA, luminanceB);
  return (lighter + 0.05) / (darker + 0.05);
}
```

**Test phase** ([index.ts, lines 240-244](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts#L240-L244)):

```typescript
test: (element, context) => {
  if (!(element instanceof HTMLElement)) return true;
  const threshold = getContrastThreshold(context.config);
  const style = window.getComputedStyle(element);
  const color = element.style.color || style.color;
  const bg = element.style.backgroundColor || style.backgroundColor;
  const ratio = contrastRatio(color, bg);
  return ratio >= threshold;
},
```

---

## 4. "Include Dark Mode" Toggle — DOES NOT EXIST

**There is NO "include dark mode" feature in the current implementation.** 

The contrast checker:
- Tests only the **currently computed styles** via `window.getComputedStyle()`
- Does **NOT** run the check twice (once for light, once for dark)
- Does **NOT** have a toggle to switch between light/dark theme colors
- Has only **one setting** for contrast thresholds: a dropdown ([index.ts, line 543](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts#L543))
  ```typescript
  {
    type: "selectbox",
    name: "contrastThreshold",
    label: "Minimum contrast ratio",
    items: [
      { value: "4.5:1", text: "4.5:1 (WCAG 2.2 default)" },
      { value: "3:1", text: "3:1 (large text / UI alternative)" },
    ],
  }
  ```

The only dark-mode reference in the codebase is a comment ([line 691](plugins/tinymce/a11y/src/index.ts#L691)):
```typescript
// way — without this the SVG default fill (black) stays black in dark mode while every
// other icon swaps.
icon.setAttribute("fill", "currentColor");
```

